// EN: image_decode_probe_corpus_sanity (`DEC-PROBE-CORPUS`, W27, TODO.md) -- regression test
//     for the `DEC-NOTHROW` (A-1) and `DEC-FORMAT-SURFACE` (A-2) findings that exercises
//     `glintfx::decode_image_file()`/`decode_png_file()` against the CONSUMER'S OWN corpus
//     bytes, generated by the adopted, verbatim `tests/tools/gen_corpus.py` (see that file's
//     own top comment for provenance: gusworld's `assets/probe-decode/gen_corpus.py`, bus
//     commit `882cae0766fb3cdf5c43410b86148aa1f87557cf`, `md5sum`-verified `cp`, byte-
//     identical below its provenance header) rather than a stand-in re-derived from a prose
//     description of the bugs -- the whole argument this item exists to generalise: "if the
//     test of the fix uses the SAME input that caught the bug, it proves the fix catches THIS
//     case; a test written from the description risks exercising a neighbour and passing for
//     the wrong reason" (`DEC-PROBE-CORPUS`, `TODO.md`).
//
//     WHERE THE CORPUS COMES FROM, AND WHY THIS FILE NEVER WRITES ONE: `tests/CMakeLists.txt`
//     runs `tests/tools/gen_corpus.py` via a `add_custom_command()` exactly ONCE, at BUILD
//     time (never at ctest time, never per-process), into a build-tree directory this
//     translation unit receives as the compiled-in `GLINTFX_PROBE_CORPUS_DIR` string (a
//     `target_compile_definitions()` value, not a `WORKING_DIRECTORY`-relative guess -- this
//     test runs correctly regardless of what CWD ctest happens to invoke it from). The
//     generated bytes are NEVER committed to this repository (only the generator is -- see
//     `gen_corpus.py`'s own provenance header) and this file itself performs ZERO writes: it
//     only opens the two fixtures the build already produced, read-only. This SIDESTEPS,
//     rather than mitigates, the W27 `.ppm`-fixed-name-in-CWD race this wave's own audit
//     found across nine other tests (three literal `"out.ppm"` collisions plus two each of
//     `"sanity_out.ppm"`/`"tex_out.ppm"`) -- there is no per-process write to race over in the
//     first place, which is a strictly stronger guarantee than giving each process its own
//     PID-suffixed path would be.
//
//     DETERMINISM, independently verified before this file was written (not merely asserted):
//     `tests/tools/gen_corpus.py <dir1>` and `... <dir2>`, run back to back, produced 31/31
//     byte-identical regular files (`md5sum`), including BOTH fixtures this file reads --
//     `png_pal_12000.png` (`c73f1af457c6d5b2fc25cac4f10db373`) and `fake_tga_garbage.png`
//     (`65c2c58c843fd97ff160031a3140436f`, whose own `sha256sum`,
//     `1dc442ea6d179c0e9f2d13f6ce1a4d68d9ff8cb7afacc514b8851a7cb93a5982`, matches the literal
//     byte array `image_png_only_sanity.cpp` already hand-embeds under the SAME provenance
//     claim -- an independent cross-check that the generator's current output is still the
//     bytes this codebase already trusted, not a silent drift).
//
//     GROUP 1 (`DEC-FORMAT-SURFACE`, A-2) -- `fake_tga_garbage.png`: an 18-byte plausible TGA
//     header (image_type=2, 4096x4096, 32bpp) followed by 64 bytes of fixed-seed noise (82
//     bytes total). 1a documents the coador this slice does not change: the GENERAL dispatch
//     (`decode_image_memory()`) still accepts it, "successfully" decoding a 4096x4096,
//     all-zero-alpha image. 1b is THE regression pin: `decode_png_file()` rejects the exact
//     same, LIVE-GENERATED bytes (`ok == false`) -- mirrors `image_png_only_sanity.cpp`'s own
//     Group 1, but sourced from the adopted generator instead of a hand-transcribed literal.
//
//     GROUP 2 (`DEC-NOTHROW`, A-1) -- `png_pal_12000.png`: the consumer's own 12000x12000
//     PALETTED PNG (144 Mpx, 576 MiB decoded RGBA8, ~212 KiB on disk because the four repeated
//     row patterns compress almost entirely away -- see that fixture's own generation comment
//     in `gen_corpus.py` for why paletted specifically forces the intermediate stb buffer
//     BELOW this library's own added `assign()` copy, the exact shape that makes `DEC-NOTHROW`
//     reproducible at all). Reuses the SAME two-stage fork()+`setrlimit(RLIMIT_AS)`
//     calibrate-then-squeeze oracle `image_decode_hardening_sanity.cpp`'s own Group B already
//     proved (STAGE 1/2 measures the REAL `VmPeak` delta an unconstrained decode of THIS
//     exact file needs; STAGE 2/2 squeezes a second child to 9/10 of that measured delta --
//     NOT the 3/4 that file's own Group B uses for its much smaller fixture, see STAGE 2/2's
//     own comment below for the measured, bisected reason the fraction does not carry over --
//     short of what STAGE 1/2 proved was needed, so an allocation inside the call must
//     genuinely fail) -- reimplemented HERE, independently, rather than shared via a common header,
//     because this file and `image_decode_hardening_sanity.cpp` are owned by different W27
//     slices editing disjoint files in the same wave (house rule against cross-file coupling
//     between parallel agents' work). Measured, on this fixture, BEFORE this file was wired
//     into the build (a throwaway probe outside the repo, linked against the already-built
//     `libglintfx.a`): calibration delta ~1099 MiB, total wall time ~1.05 s, peak RSS ~1.1
//     GiB -- comfortably inside the self-hosted heavy runner's 8 GiB cap (`AGENTS.md`) and
//     fast enough to run on every `ctest` invocation, not just on demand.
//
//     `probe_mem.cpp` (the bus's OTHER file, same commit, `assets/probe-decode/`) was NOT
//     adopted byte-for-byte the way `gen_corpus.py` was -- see `gen_corpus.py`'s own
//     provenance header for why. Its ~50-line METHOD is cited here instead: read a process's
//     own `VmHWM`/`VmPeak` from `/proc/self/status`, run exactly ONE decode call inside a
//     `try` that wraps only it, and report the `typeid` of any exception that escapes. STAGE
//     1/2 below follows that same shape (measure peak virtual-memory growth around a single
//     decode call) but reads `VmPeak` rather than `VmHWM` (matching, not diverging from, what
//     `image_decode_hardening_sanity.cpp`'s own Group B already established and proved works
//     for this exact oracle -- see that file's own history in its top comment for why `VmHWM`
//     alone under-measured a transient peak the two-stage design needs to reproduce). The
//     `typeid`-on-catch half of `probe_mem.cpp`'s technique is unnecessary here: this oracle's
//     observable is the PARENT's `waitpid()`-and-`WIFSIGNALED()` check on the child (an
//     uncaught `std::bad_alloc` -> `std::terminate()` -> `abort()` -> `SIGABRT`, the exact
//     `DEC-NOTHROW` regression this test exists to catch), not a same-process `catch` clause.
//
//     Runs UNCONDITIONALLY, in BOTH build configurations -- no RmlUi/GL/window dependency
//     whatsoever, same "nothing display-related to isolate here" reasoning as
//     image_decode_sanity.cpp/image_sanity.cpp/image_decode_hardening_sanity.cpp above. Linux-
//     only (`/proc/self/status`, `fork()`, `setrlimit()`), matching this whole library's
//     "Linux x86-64" platform scope (`CLAUDE.md`) -- no `#ifdef` needed. Registered ONLY when
//     `tests/CMakeLists.txt`'s own configure-time Python3+Pillow capability check succeeds
//     (`gen_corpus.py` imports `PIL.Image` unconditionally at module scope, for fixtures this
//     file does not even read -- the two fixtures THIS file needs, `png_pal_12000.png` and
//     `fake_tga_garbage.png`, are built by the script's own hand-rolled `raw_png()`/PNG-chunk
//     helpers with no PIL dependency, but they sit downstream, in file order, of several
//     `PIL.Image.new()` calls the unmodified, adopted script runs first -- so reaching either
//     fixture still requires Pillow to be importable, even though neither fixture's own bytes
//     depend on it); see `tests/CMakeLists.txt`'s own comment on that gate, and its
//     `message(WARNING ...)`, for what happens when the capability check fails (this target is
//     simply not registered -- an honest absence in the configure log, never a silent skip
//     inside a test that claims to have run).
// PT: image_decode_probe_corpus_sanity (`DEC-PROBE-CORPUS`, W27, TODO.md) -- teste de
//     regressão para os achados `DEC-NOTHROW` (A-1) e `DEC-FORMAT-SURFACE` (A-2) que exercita
//     `glintfx::decode_image_file()`/`decode_png_file()` contra os PRÓPRIOS bytes de corpus do
//     consumidor, gerados pelo `tests/tools/gen_corpus.py` adotado, verbatim (ver o próprio
//     comentário de topo daquele arquivo pra proveniência: `assets/probe-decode/gen_corpus.py`
//     do gusworld, commit do bus `882cae0766fb3cdf5c43410b86148aa1f87557cf`, `cp` verificado
//     por `md5sum`, byte-idêntico abaixo do próprio cabeçalho de proveniência) em vez de um
//     substituto re-derivado de uma descrição em prosa dos bugs -- o argumento inteiro que
//     este item existe pra generalizar: "se o teste do conserto usar a MESMA entrada que
//     pegou o bug, ele prova que o conserto pega ESTE caso; um teste escrito da descrição
